A||||7||kong||hey ogre, help!! clutch prob||||1||
Z||000000||kong||02-09-2001||11:31 PM||||Hey Ogre, I hope you're out there. I was driving around today and my fiero started shifting hard, and in about 3 miles my clutch wouldn't disengage. I stopped and checked the master for fluid, and it was right where it was supposed to be. <BR> I had a guy at a gas station push the clutch pedal for me to check for travel on the slave and T.O. arm. Plenty of movement there too. No leaks anywhere that I can see.<BR> <BR>I had to shut the car off at every stop sign and signal. Put it in gear and start it in first gear to get home. Got any suggestions? I searched through the archives for a while and couldn't find, or didn't see anything for this one. HELP!!!!    Thanks ,,,Kong||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-10-2001||01:42 PM||||sounds like the hardware on the tranny. the arm can bend and not move far enough to release. could be loose. hard to say w/o seeing it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||02-10-2001||02:55 PM||||I had the same problem.. it would shift REALLY REALLY hard into 1st ,2nd and reverse.. i tried all the fix's found on this forum, new slave cylinder, new master cylinder, bleeding the slave, new clutch pedal and bushings.. nothing worked.. last weekend put in a new clutch and throwout bearing... now it shifts like a dream  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Chance||02-10-2001||07:20 PM||||I have the EXACT same problem with my 86GT 5sp.... I am taking it in Monday to have it fixed.  Before it got to the "shut off at stops and power-shift" stage, It was getting harder to get into gear, and not completly releaseing when the pedal was pushed.  One night, I was comming to a stop sign, pushed the clutch to the floor, and could feel SOMETHING give. From then on, I had to put it in gear before I started it.  I THINK its the clutch fork, but I will let you all know what I find out.||||reg||3
Z||000004||GT GT 87||02-10-2001||11:07 PM||||I once had a similar problem - clutch pedal felt fine, good movment at slave cyl, and clutch arm ok.But the clutch wouldn't release fully,really bad at stop to put in gear.I finally gave in and had the clutch changed at 110,000 Mi. When I looked at the returned old parts ,there was plenty of life left on the disc ,but a part of the disc that holds the takeup springs in place had broken off and let one of the springs to turn sideways and even with the pedal in the spring still dragged on the flywheel making the clutch still somewhat engaded,and hard to put in gear!!!!!!!!!!!!                      STEVE||||reg||1
Z||000005||kong||02-11-2001||01:38 AM|||| Yeah guys, that's what I was afraid of. Chance let me know what you find out about yours. I'm gonna tear mine apart next weekend. I'm NOT looking forward to it, but, it's my daily driver, gotta get it fixed.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Chance||02-11-2001||06:39 AM||||No Problem, I will let you know.  I still think it was because of the last shop I took it to who replaced it a 2 years ago didn't put it in right.  After that ordeal, and calling around trying to find someone, I came to the conclusion that there is NO ONE in Joplin Missouri who has replaced a Fiero clutch, and if they have, mine would be their second time they have and they really don't want to do it, or want to charge me 1200 bucks like the first shop.  I wish I had the tools, and a shop to do it myself, or some of you guys out there lived closer!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||kong||02-21-2001||02:42 PM||||y'all were right. changed the pressure plate,clutch,and T.O. And it practically falls into gear now. It took me 7 hrs to do it, and I'm glad it's over. the next time something this big goes wrong, I'm dropping the whole cradle and a 3.4 is going in!||||reg||1
